ID:32555229\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33009001\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033029 \"An OFF calbindin-positive bipolar cell that has a large dendritic field and stratifies narrowly close to the middle of the inner plexiform layer. Its axon terminal is characterized by regularly branching and varicose processes resembling beads on a string. Most of DB3a contacts with cones are triad-associated.\")\n32393:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033029 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32394:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033029 \"2023-04-04T10:53:33Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32395:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.3389/fnana.2015.00122\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033029 \"DB3 cell\")\n32396:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033029 \"DB3a cell\")\n32397:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"DOI:10.3389/fnana.2015.00122\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033029 \"Originally, DB3a cells were termed diffuse bipolar 3 (DB3) cells. When an additional bipolar type which stratifies slightly more vitread and is calbindin negative was detected, this cell was renamed diffuse bipolar 3a cell. The axons of neighboring DB3a cells make homologous gap junctions. The DB3a cells provide the majority of their output to OFF parasol cells.\")\n32398:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033029 \"diffuse bipolar 3a cell\")\n32399:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033029 obo:CL_0000750)\n32401:# Class: obo:CL_4033030 (diffuse bipolar 3b cell)\n32403:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32555229\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033030 \"An OFF calbindin-negative bipolar cell that has a large dendritic field and stratifies narrowly close to the middle of the inner plexiform layer. Its axon terminal is characterized by regularly branching and varicose processes resembling beads on a string. Most of DB3b contacts with cones are non-triad-associated.\")\n32404:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033030 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32405:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033030 \"2023-04-04T10:53:42Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32406:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033030 \"DB3b cell\")\n32407:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24107939\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33009001\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033030 \"In humans, a DB3b cell is CD15 positive. A DB3b cell might make sparse contacts to rod photoreceptors.\")\n32408:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033030 \"diffuse bipolar 3b cell\")\n32409:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033030 obo:CL_0000750)\n32411:# Class: obo:CL_4033031 (diffuse bipolar 4 cell)\n32413:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27833534\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32555229\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033031 \"An ON diffuse bipolar cell that predominantly connects to ON parasol cells and lateral amacrine cells.\")\n32414:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033031 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32415:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033031 \"2023-04-04T09:51:10Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32416:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033031 \"DB4 cell\")\n32417:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033031 \"diffuse bipolar 4 cell\")\n32418:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033031 obo:CL_0000749)\n32420:# Class: obo:CL_4033032 (diffuse bipolar 6 cell)\n32422:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXr