onym obo:CL_4033052 \"inner parasol cell\")\n32643:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033052 \"ON parasol ganglion cell\")\n32644:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4033052 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_4023032 obo:CL_4023189))\n32646:# Class: obo:CL_4033053 (small bistratified retinal ganglion cell)\n32648:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033053 \"A bistratfied retinal ganglion cell with a small dendritic field that has dendrites in the ON and OFF sublamina of the retinal inner plexiform layer and carries blue-ON/yellow-OFF signals. This cell receives bipolar and amacrine input to both the OFF and ON dendritic tree.\")\n32649:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033053 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32650:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033053 \"2023-08-08T12:43:56Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32651:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033053 \"small bistratified cell\")\n32652:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1002/cne.22183\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033053 \"small bistratified cell, blue-ON/yellow-OFF ganglion cell\")\n32653:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033053 \"Polyak's shrub cell\")\n32654:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033053 \"SBS ganglion cell\")\n32655:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34093409\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033053 \"sbRGC\")\n32656:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033053 \"small bistratified retinal ganglion cell\")\n32657:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033053 obo:CL_0003001)\n32658:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033053 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0001792))\n32660:# Class: obo:CL_4033054 (perivascular cell)\n32662:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24928499\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27889329\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033054 \"A cell that is adjacent to a vessel. A perivascular cell plays a crucial role in maintaining vascular function and tissue homeostasis. This cell type regulates vessel integrity and flow dynamics.\")\n32663:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033054 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32664:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033054 \"2023-08-22T13:40:28Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32665:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033054 \"perivascular cell\")\n32666:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4033054 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002220 obo:UBERON_0002049)))\n32668:# Class: obo:CL_4033055 (airway submucosal gland duct multiciliated cell)\n32670:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17707699\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30864819\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033055 \"A multi-ciliated epithelial cell located in ciliated duct of an airway submucosal gland, characterized by a columnar shape and motile cilia on its apical surface.\")\n32671:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033055 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32672:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033055 <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9185-3994>)\n32673:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033055 \"2023-09-08T10:32:27Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32674:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033055 \"airway submucosal gland duct ciliated cell\")\n32675:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033055 \"airway submucosal gland duct multiciliated cell\")\n32676:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4033055 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000075 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_8410077) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_8600014) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0031514) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0010007)))\n32678:# Class: obo:CL_4033056 (onychocyte)\n32680:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24079581\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28098391\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30969555\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34099859\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39451193\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033056 \"A terminally differentiated, specialized keratinocyte originating primarily from the nail matrix. During onychokeratinization, these cells undergo progressive flattening and produce high levels of hard, disulfide cross-linked keratins (Eckhart et al., 2024) that form the rigid, compact nail plate. Unlike epidermal keratinocytes, onychocytes are firmly integrated into the nail plate and do not desquamate.\")\n32681:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033056 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32682:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033056 \"2023-10-03T12:49:46Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32683:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033056 \"onychocyte\")\n32684:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033056 obo:CL_0000312)\n32685:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033056 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0008198))\n32687:# Class: obo:CL_4033057 (luminal adaptive secretory precursor cell of mammary gland)\n32689:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19648928\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35617956\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://nrs.harvard.edu/URN-3:HUL.INSTREPOS:37368328\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033057 \"A luminal epithelial cell of the mammary gland that can proliferate and has the potential to differentiate into a lactocyte during pregnancy. In humans, a luminal adaptive secretory precursor cell can be identified by high levels of the markers EpCAM and CD49f, and in mice it can be identified by low levels of CD29 and high levels of CD14, Kit, CD61, and Tspan8.\")\n32690:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033057 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32691:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033057 <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4969-670X>)\n32692:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033057 \"2023-10-13T13:02:55Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32693:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35617956\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"alveolar cell\")\n32694:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26390871\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"alveolar progenitor\")\n32695:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1101/2023.04.21.537845\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"luminal progenitor\")\n32696:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20346151\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"luminal progenitor cell\")\n32697:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37380767\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"luminal secretory cell\")\n32698:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://nrs.harvard.edu/URN-3:HUL.INSTREPOS:37368328\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"ER-negative luminal alveolar progenitor\")\n32699:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://nrs.harvard.edu/URN-3:HUL.INSTREPOS:37368328\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"AP\")\n32700:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35617956\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"AV\")\n32701:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"LASP\")\n32702:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1101/2023.04.21.537845\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"LP\")\n32703:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37380767\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"LumSec\")\n32704:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033057 \"luminal adaptive secretory precursor cell of mammary gland\")\n32705:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033057 obo:CL_0002326)\n32706:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033057 obo:CL_0011115)\n32708:# Class: obo:CL_4033058 (luminal hormone-sensing cell of mammary gland)\n32710:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19648928\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26390871\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34156490\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://nrs.harvard.edu/URN-3:HUL.INSTREPOS:37368328\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033058 \"A luminal epithelial cell of the mammary gland that transduces endocrine cues to orchestrate proliferation, architectural remodeling, and differentiation of other cells in the mammary gland via paracrine signaling. This cell expresses high levels of estrogen receptors. In humans, a luminal hormone-sensing cell can be identified by high levels of EpCAM and low levels of CD49f, and in mice it can be identified by low levels of CD29 and high levels of Foxa1, CD133, and Sca1 (Ly6a).\")\n32711:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033058 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32712:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033058 <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4969-670X>)\n32713:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033058 \"2023-10-16T08:30:25Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32714:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1101/2023.04.21.537845\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033058 \"hormone sensing cell\")\n32715:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26390871\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033058 \"hormone-sensing mammary epithelial cell\")\n32716:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37380767\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033058 \"luminal hormone-responsive cell\")\n32717:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20346151\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033058 \"luminal mature cell\")\n32718:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://nrs.harvard.edu/URN-3:HUL.INSTREPOS:37368328\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033058 \"ER-positive luminal hormone-sensor cell\")\n32719:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1101/2023.04.21.537845\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033058 \"HS\")\n32720:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26390871\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033058 \"HS-MEC\")\n32721:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033058 \"LHS\")\n32722:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37380767\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033058 \"LumHR\")\n32723:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26390871\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34156490\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4969-670X\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033058 \"Following lineage specification, a luminal hormone-sensing cell expresses receptors for one or more hormones, such as estrogens, progesterone, androgens, and prolactin. In response to progesterone, luminal hormone-sensing cells express TNFSF11, WNT4, and RSPO1, among other factors, which cause branching, proliferation, and partial differentiation in LASP and B-Myo cells during luteal phases of the estrous/menstrual cycle and during gestation. During ductal elongation, ER activity drives expression of AREG in LHS cells, which is necessary for proliferation of the epithelium to fill the mammary fat pad.\")\n32724:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033058 \"luminal hormone-sensing cell of mammary gland\")\n32725:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033058 obo:CL_0002326)\n32726:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033058 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002104 obo:PR_000007204))\n32728:# Class: obo:CL_4033059 (lactocyte type 1)\n32730:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35091553\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35377806\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033059 \"A lactocyte that highly expresses genes associated with transcription, immune cell function, and cellular stress. A lactocyte type 1 also expresses genes involved in milk component biosynthesis (e.g., LALBA and CSNs), albeit at lower levels than a lactocyte type 2.\")\n32731:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033059 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32732:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033059 <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4361-817X>)\n32733:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033059 \"2023-10-16T13:15:36Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32734:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34097179\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033059 \"luminal cluster 1 cell\")\n32735:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35091553\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033059 \"LC1\")\n32736:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35091553\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033059 \"LMC major luminal cluster 1\")\n32737:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35091553\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033059 \"progenitor MEC\")\n32738:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033059 \"lactocyte type 1\")\n32739:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033059 obo:CL_0002325)\n32741:# Class: obo:CL_4033060 (lactocyte type 2)\n32743:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35091553\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35377806\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033060 \"A lactocyte that highly expresses genes associated with lipid production and milk component biosynthesis.\")\n32744:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033060 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32745:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033060 <https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4361-817X>)\n32746:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033060 \"2023-10-16T13:15:55Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32747:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35377806\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033060 \"luminal cluster 2 cell\")\n32748:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35091553\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033060 \"LC2\")\n32749:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35091553\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033060 \"LMC major luminal cluster 2\")\n32750:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033060 \"lactocyte type 2\")\n32751:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033060 obo:CL_0002325)\n32753:# Class: obo:CL_4033061 (endothelial cell of central vein of liver)\n32755:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28287163\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033061 \"An endothelial cell that is part of a central vein of liver.\")\n32756:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033061 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32757:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28287163\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033061 \"endothelial cell of central vein\")\n32758:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033061 \"endothelial cell of central vein of liver\")\n32759:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4033061 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000115 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0006841)))\n32761:# Class: obo:CL_4033062 (interstitial extravillous trophoblast cell)\n32763:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37630754\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1007/978-3-030-84725-8\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033062 \"A trophoblast cell that invades the uterine wall to anchor the placenta to the uterus. An interstitial extravillous trophoblast cell differentiates from an extravillous trophoblast cell, becoming hyperchromatic and changing its morphology to a fibroblast-like spindle-shaped cell. In humans, this cell can be distinguished by the expression of placental-specific protein 8, which stimulates migration.\")\n32764:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033062 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32765:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033062 \"2024-01-08T15:43:15Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32766:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1007/978-3-030-84725-8\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033062 \"invasive interstitial extravillous trophoblast cell\")\n32767:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37630754\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033062 \"iEVT\")\n32768:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37630754\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033062 \"interstitial extravillous trophoblast\")\n32769:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11337369\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033062 \"interstitial trophoblast\")\n32770:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033062 \"interstitial extravillous trophoblast cell\")\n32771:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033062 obo:CL_0000351)\n32772:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033062 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0008036))\n32774:# Class: obo:CL_4033063 (endovascular extravillous trophoblast cell)\n32776:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37630754\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1007/978-3-030-84725-8\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033063 \"A trophoblast cell that invades the maternal spiral arteries and replace the endothelial lining, remodeling the vessels and allowing for adequate blood transport into the placenta. An endovascular extravillous trophoblast cell differentiates from an extravillous trophoblast cell. In humans, this cell can be distinguished by the expression of CD56.\")\n32777:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033063 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32778:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033063 \"2024-01-08T15:43:32Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32779:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37630754\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033063 \"eEVT\")\n32780:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37630754\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033063 \"endovascular extravillous trophoblast\")\n32781:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11337369\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033063 \"endovascular trophoblast\")\n32782:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37630754\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033063 \"Shortly after implantation, the endovascular extravillous trophoblast cells occlude the maternal spiral arteries, preventing premature oxygen delivery to the placental villi and reducing fetal oxidative stress.\")\n32783:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033063 \"endovascular extravillous trophoblast cell\")\n32784:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033063 obo:CL_0000351)\n32785:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033063 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0008036))\n32787:# Class: obo:CL_4033064 (uterine resident macrophage)\n32789:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36113384\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033064 \"A tissue-resident macrophage that is part of the uterus.\")\n32790:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033064 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32791:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033064 \"2024-01-08T16:05:09Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32792:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36113384\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033064 \"uterine macrophage\")\n32793:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36113384\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033064 \"Uterine macrophages are reported to be evenly distributed throughout the endometrial stroma but with aggregations observed close to the lumen of superficial secretory glands.\")\n32794:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033064 \"uterine resident macrophage\")\n32795:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4033064 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000864 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000995)))\n32797:# Class: obo:CL_4033065 (preplasmablast)\n32799:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21918187\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30755708\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33150420\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033065 \"A mature B cell that serves as an intermediate stage in the differentiation of naive B cells into a plasmablast. A preplasmablast expresses CD30 and IL-6R and lacks expression of CD20, CD23, CD38 and CD138.\")\n32800:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033065 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32801:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033065 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833>)\n32802:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033065 \"2024-04-25T09:14:58Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32803:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23613519\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033065 \"pre-plasmablast\")\n32804:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33661294\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033065 \"preplasmablastic cell\")\n32805:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21918187\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033065 \"prePB\")\n32806:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033065 \"preplasmablast\")\n32807:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033065 obo:CL_0000785)\n32808:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033065 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000788))\n32809:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033065 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002203 obo:CL_0000980))\n32811:# Class: obo:CL_4033066 (pre-granulosa cell)\n32813:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17639032\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32759216\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33970370\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38178246\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033066 \"A supporting cell that is part of the ovary and differentiates into a granulosa cell. A pre-granulosa cell develops from an early supporting gonadal cell by repressing testis determination, which can then proliferate to form primordial follicles.\")\n32814:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033066 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32815:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033066 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833>)\n32816:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033066 \"2024-06-07T12:04:57Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32817:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32759216\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033066 \"ovarian pregranulosa cell\")\n32818:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17639032\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32759216\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033066 \"pregranulosa cell\")\n32819:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32759216\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033066 \"PG cell\")\n32820:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033066 \"pre-granulosa cell\")\n32821:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033066 obo:CL_0000630)\n32822:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033066 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000992))\n32823:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033066 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002210 obo:CL_4033083))\n32825:# Class: obo:CL_4033067 (mural granulosa cell)\n32827:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27815559\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33970370\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34198768\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033067 \"A follicular cell of ovary that differentiates from a cuboidal granulosa cell during the secondary follicle stage. Mural granulosa cells line the inner surface of the follicle wall, surrounding the fluid-filled antral cavity. These cells produce oestrogen during the follicular phase in response to follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH), and progesterone after ovulation in response to luteinizing hormone (LH).\")\n32828:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033067 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32829:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033067 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833>)\n32830:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033067 \"2024-06-07T12:15:13Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32831:AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasDbXref obo:CL_4033067 \"EFO:0005289\")\n32832:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1530/REP-16-0500\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033067 \"MGC\")\n32833:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34198768\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033067 \"mural GC\")\n32834:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033067 \"mural granulosa cell\")\n32835:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033067 obo:CL_0000501)\n32836:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033067 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000992))\n32837:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033067 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_4033084))\n32839:# Class: obo:CL_4033083 (squamous granulosa cell)\n32841:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28892263\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033083 \"A granulosa cell that has a squamous morphology and form a single layer around the oocyte in primordial follicles. This cell develops directly into a cuboidal granulosa cell during the primordial-to-primary follicle transition.\")\n32842:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033083 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32843:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033083 \"2024-09-24T13:13:24Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32844:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22402964\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033083 \"flattened granulosa cell\")\n32845:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33914868\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033083 \"pre-granulosa cell\")\n32846:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33914868\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033083 \"squamous GC\")\n32847:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033083 \"Often in literature squamous granulosa cell and pre-granulosa cell are used as synonyms. However, this term only makes reference to the quiescent granulosa cells that surround the primordial ovarian follicle, while a pre-granulosa cell proliferates to form the primordial follicle (and thus cells become the squamous granulosa cells).\")\n32848:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033083 \"squamous granulosa cell\")\n32849:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033083 obo:CL_0000501)\n32850:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033083 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0003981))\n32851:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033083 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002207 obo:CL_4033066))\n32852:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033083 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002210 obo:CL_4033084))\n32854:# Class: obo:CL_4033084 (cuboidal granulosa cell)\n32856:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28892263\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033084 \"A granulosa cell that has a cuboidal morphology and develops from squamous granulosa cell during the transition between primordial follicle to primary follicle. Cuboidal granulosa cells proliferate to form a second layer within secondary follicles.\")\n32857:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033084 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32858:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033084 \"2024-09-24T13:14:57Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32859:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19001500\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033084 \"columnar granulosa cell\")\n32860:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31849844\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033084 \"cuboidal epithelial granulosa cell\")\n32861:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19001500\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033084 \"columnar GC\")\n32862:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33914868\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033084 \"cuboidal GC\")\n32863:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033084 \"cuboidal granulosa cell\")\n32864:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033084 obo:CL_0000501)\n32865:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033084 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001305))\n32866:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033084 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002207 obo:CL_4033083))\n32868:# Class: obo:CL_4033085 (diffuse bipolar 5 cell)\n32870:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27833534\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033085 \"An ON diffuse bipolar cell that stratifies in the stratum 3 of the inner plexiform layer to make synapses with ON parasol ganglion cells. A diffuse bipolar 5 cell has high expression of MYO16 compared with other bipolar cells.\")\n32871:AnnotationAssertion(obo:RO_0002175 obo:CL_4033085 obo:NCBITaxon_9443)\n32872:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033085 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32873:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033085 \"2024-10-16T12:46:53Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32874:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32032773\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033085 \"DB5 cell\")\n32875:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27833534\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033085 \"A diffuse bipolar 5 cell typically contacts 7–8 cone photoreceptors. The number and thickness of its dendritic processes are intermediate between those of a diffuse bipolar 6 cell (less dense and thinner) and a diffuse bipolar 4 cell (denser and thicker).\")\n32876:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033085 \"diffuse bipolar 5 cell\")\n32877:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033085 obo:CL_0000749)\n32879:# Class: obo:CL_4033086 (lipid-associated macrophage)\n32881:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31257031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34876704\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35712121\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033086 \"A tissue-resident macrophage that is associated with lipids. This cell responsible of anti-inflammatory functions, lipid accumulation and enhancing phagocytosis (Wculek et al., 2022, Liu et al., 2022). In mice and humans, a lipid-associated macrophage is characterized by the marker Trem2 (Jaitlin et al., 2019).\")\n32882:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033086 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32883:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033086 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8134-3037>)\n32884:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033086 \"2024-10-17T10:20:13Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32885:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31257031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033086 \"LAM\")\n32886:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35021063\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37153549\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033086 \"Distinct from “adipose macrophage” in Trem2 expression, and is not limited to adipose tissue. Guilliams et al. describe these cells as being distinct from Kupffer cells.\")\n32887:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033086 \"lipid-associated macrophage\")\n32888:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033086 obo:CL_0000235)\n32889:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033086 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000016626))\n32891:# Class: obo:CL_4033087 (placental resident macrophage)\n32893:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39007150\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033087 \"A tissue-resident macrophage that is part of the placenta. This cell helps preventing immunological rejection of the fetus by modulating the immune environment. A placental resident macrophage has high plasticity to adapt to the changing needs of each phase of pregnancy.\")\n32894:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033087 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32895:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033087 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833>)\n32896:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033087 \"2024-10-31T10:24:21Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32897:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39007150\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033087 \"placental macrophage\")\n32898:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033087 \"placental resident macrophage\")\n32899:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4033087 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000864 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0001987)))\n32901:# Class: obo:CL_4033088 (decidual resident macrophage)\n32903:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39007150\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033088 \"A resident macrophage that is part of the decidua. Some decidual macrophages are derived from maternal blood monocytes that are recruited to the uterus shortly after conception. The main functions of a decidual macrophage are implantation, placental development, immune regulation and vascular remodeling.\")\n32904:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033088 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32905:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033088 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833>)\n32906:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033088 \"2024-10-31T10:33:04Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32907:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39007150\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033088 \"decidual macrophage\")\n32908:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39007150\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033088 \"maternal decidual macrophage\")\n32909:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033088 \"decidual resident macrophage\")\n32910:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033088 obo:CL_4033087)\n32911:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033088 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002450))\n32913:# Class: obo:CL_4033089 (atretic follicular cell of ovary)\n32915:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38069168\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033089 \"A follicular cell of ovary that has begun to degenerate and undergo atresia, a specialized apoptosis. This cell is found in an atretic follicle, which is an ovarian follicle that started to mature but failed to reach full development and instead regresses.\")\n32916:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033089 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32917:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033089 \"2024-11-05T11:23:25Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32918:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033089 \"atretic follicular cell of ovary\")\n32919:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4033089 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0002174 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000056 obo:GO_0001552)))\n32921:# Class: obo:CL_4033090 (atretic granulosa cell)\n32923:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15353131\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:38069168\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033090 \"A granulosa cell that is undergoing atresia. This cell type displays distinct morphological alterations compared with a healthy granulosa cell, including pyknosis (nuclear condensation) and cellular shrinkage.\")\n32924:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033090 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32925:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033090 \"2024-11-05T11:25:28Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32926:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15353131\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033090 \"apoptotic granulosa cell\")\n32927:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033090 \"atretic granulosa cell\")\n32928:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033090 obo:CL_4033089)\n32929:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033090 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:CL_0000501))\n32931:# Class: obo:CL_4033091 (glycinergic-GABAergic amacrine cell)\n32933:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37124720\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033091 \"An amacrine cell that uses both GABA and glycine as neurotransmitters.\")\n32934:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033091 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32935:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033091 \"2024-12-02T13:44:17Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32936:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37124720\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033091 \"glycinergic/GABAergic amacrine neuron\")\n32937:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033091 \"glycinergic-GABAergic amacrine cell\")\n32938:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4033091 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000561 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061537)))\n32940:# Class: obo:CL_4033092 (CD57-positive enterocyte)\n32942:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37468586\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033092 \"An enterocyte that is part of a duodenal epithelium and expresses beta-1,3-glucuronyltransferase 1 (B3GAT1), also known as CD57 or HNK-1.\")\n32943:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033092 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32944:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033092 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833>)\n32945:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033092 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9961-7673>)\n32946:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033092 \"2024-12-06T14:32:49Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32947:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37468586\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033092 \"CD57+ enterocyte\")\n32948:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37468586\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4033092 \"While CD57 is traditionally associated with immune cells (e.g., NK cells), its expression on enterocytes marks unique epithelial subsets with specific functions or maturation states. These cells are specially enriched in areas of the duodenum within submucosal glands.\")\n32949:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033092 \"CD57-positive enterocyte\")\n32950:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4033092 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000584 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0008346) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001440)))\n32952:# Class: obo:CL_4033093 (limbal epithelial stem cell of cornea)\n32954:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20614614\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29105366\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36983561\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37768272\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033093 \"A stem cell that is part of the corneo-scleral limbus. This cell type resides at the basal layer of the epithelium and has a small size and high nuclear to cytoplasmatic ratio (Secker and Daniels, 2009). A limbal stem cell is responsible for corneal epithelial renewal and repair (Li et al., 2023), and to help maintain a clear corneal surface by preventing conjunctival epithelial cells from migrating onto the cornea (Wang et al., 2023).\")\n32955:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033093 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32956:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033093 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833>)\n32957:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033093 \"2024-12-11T13:59:19Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32958:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20614614\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033093 \"limbal epithelial stem cell\")\n32959:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17562792\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033093 \"limbal stem cell\")\n32960:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20614614\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033093 \"LESC\")\n32961:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36983561\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033093 \"LSC\")\n32962:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033093 \"limbal epithelial stem cell of cornea\")\n32963:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4033093 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000034 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0006761)))\n32964:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033093 obo:CL_0000036)\n32965:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033093 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0000482))\n32966:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033093 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002203 obo:CL_0000575))\n32968:# Class: obo:CL_4033094 (age-associated B cell)\n32970:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30873171\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31986068\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35298565\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35798993\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033094 \"A transcriptionally distinct memory B cell whose presence increases with age, during infections, and in autoimmune diseases. In humans and mice, this cell type can be identified by the expression of T-bet, CD11c, CD11b, and the lack of CD21. An age-associated B cell responds to TLR stimuli, may produce autoantibodies, and participates in antiviral responses and pathogen clearance.\")\n32971:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033094 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32972:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033094 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833>)\n32973:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033094 \"2025-01-08T14:44:57Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32974:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35798993\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033094 \"ABC\")\n32975:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033094 \"age-associated B cell\")\n32976:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033094 obo:CL_0000787)\n32978:# Class: obo:CL_4033095 (diffuse bipolar 4a cell)\n32980:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31995762\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1101/2023.11.07.566105\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033095 \"An ON bipolar cell that has high expression of DIRC3, KCNJ3, LINC01915, PTPRK compared with other bipolar cells.\")\n32981:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033095 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32982:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033095 \"2025-01-14T13:48:42Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32983:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1101/2023.11.07.566105\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033095 \"DB4a\")\n32984:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033095 \"diffuse bipolar 4a cell\")\n32985:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033095 obo:CL_0000749)\n32986:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033095 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9606))\n32988:# Class: obo:CL_4033096 (diffuse bipolar 4b cell)\n32990:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31995762\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1101/2023.11.07.566105\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033096 \"An ON bipolar cell that has high expression of NOS1AP compared with other bipolar cells.\")\n32991:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033096 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n32992:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033096 \"2025-01-14T13:49:08Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n32993:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1101/2023.11.07.566105\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033096 \"DB4b\")\n32994:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033096 \"diffuse bipolar 4b cell\")\n32995:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033096 obo:CL_0000749)\n32996:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033096 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002162 obo:NCBITaxon_9606))\n32998:# Class: obo:CL_4033097 (Schlemm's canal endothelial cell)\n33000:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25051267\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25223880\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033097 \"A specialised endothelial cell that is part of the canal of Schlemm. This cell type shares characteristics and expresses markers of both blood and lymphatic endothelial cells (Kizhatil et al., 2014) and regulates aqueous humor outflow resistance by modulating pore formation and responding to mechanical strain (Stamer et al., 2015).\")\n33001:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033097 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n33002:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033097 \"2025-06-16T13:55:29Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n33003:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25051267\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033097 \"SC endothelial cell\")\n33004:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25051267\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033097 \"SEC\")\n33005:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033097 \"Schlemm's canal endothelial cell\")\n33006:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26402712\") Annotation(rdfs:comment \"Schematic of the conventional outflow pathway, showing the Schlemm's canal (SC, green) and the trabecular meshwork (TM, orange). The left inset shows an expanded view of the Schlemm’s canal’s microanatomy detailing the cell morphology of the inner and outer wall endocrine cells.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4033097 \"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Schlemms_canal_endo_cell_PMID26402712.png\"^^xsd:anyURI)\n33007:EquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4033097 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000115 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0004029)))\n33009:# Class: obo:CL_4033098 (inner wall Schlemm's canal endothelial cell)\n33011:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15454474\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26402712\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033098 \"A Schlemm's canal endothelial cell that lines the inner wall of the Schlemm's canal. This cell exhibits a cobblestone appearance due to the significant biomechanical load it experiences, as well as the segmental flow of aqueous humor. The degree of biomechanical stress can lead to the formation of dome-like outpouchings known as giant vacuoles. In addition, the cell contains transcellular pores that mediate aqueous humor transport (Dautriche et al., 2015). This endothelial cell also displays prominent peripheral F-actin bands which help maintain structural integrity under pressure (Ethier et al., 2004).\")\n33012:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033098 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n33013:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033098 \"2025-06-17T13:33:32Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n33014:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26402712\") oboInOwl:hasNarrowSynonym obo:CL_4033098 \"human Schlemm's canal inner wall cell\")\n33015:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26402712\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033098 \"HSCIW cell\")\n33016:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033098 \"inner wall Schlemm's canal endothelial cell\")\n33017:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26402712\") Annotation(rdfs:comment \"Schematic of the conventional outflow pathway, showing the Schlemm's canal (SC, green) and the trabecular meshwork (TM, orange). The left inset shows an expanded view of the Schlemm’s canal’s microanatomy detailing the cell morphology of the inner and outer wall endocrine cells. The inner wall endocrine cells, shown in blue, line the canal surface facing the trabecular meshwork. Some of the inner wall cells contain giant vacuoles.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4033098 \"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Schlemms_canal_endo_cell_PMID26402712.png\"^^xsd:anyURI)\n33018:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033098 obo:CL_4033097)\n33019:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033098 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_0046930))\n33021:# Class: obo:CL_4033099 (outer wall Schlemm's canal endothelial cell)\n33023:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:1426078\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15454474\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26402712\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033099 \"A Schlemm's canal endothelial cell that lines the outer wall of the Schlemm's canal. This cell displays a smooth and flat morphology (Dautriche et al., 2015) and it is distinguished by the presence of Weibel-Palade bodies, specialized organelles that produce, store, and release P-Selectin (Hamanaka et al., 1992). This endothelial cell also exhibits stellate (star-shaped) actin arrangements distributed throughout much of the cell (Ethier et al., 2004).\")\n33024:AnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4033099 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6677-8489>)\n33025:AnnotationAssertion(terms:date obo:CL_4033099 \"2025-06-17T13:33:41Z\"^^xsd:dateTime)\n33026:AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4033099 \"outer wall Schlemm's canal endothelial cell\")\n33027:AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(dc:license <http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26402712\") Annotation(rdfs:comment \"Schematic of the conventional outflow pathway, showing the Schlemm's canal (SC, green) and the trabecular meshwork (TM, orange). The left inset shows an expanded view of the Schlemm’s canal’s microanatomy detailing the cell morphology of the inner and outer wall endocrine cells. The outer wall endocrine cells, shown in green, line the side of Schlemm’s canal facing the collector channels and venous system.\") foaf:depiction obo:CL_4033099 \"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/cl/images/Schlemms_canal_endo_cell_PMID26402712.png\"^^xsd:anyURI)\n33028:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033099 obo:CL_4033097)\n33029:SubClassOf(obo:CL_4033099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000051 obo:GO_003